{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n  Quicksort\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <limits.h>\\n#include <openssl/md5.h>\\n\\n#define INSERTION_SORT_CUTOFF 24\\n#define PARALLEL_SORT_LIMIT 262144\\n#define TASK_SORT_LIMIT 32768\\n\\n/*\\n * Prototypes\\n */\\nvoid srandnum(int seed);\\ndouble randnum(void);\\nint *generate_case(int N);\\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax);\\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j);\\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N);\\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N);\\n\\nstatic int sort_depth_limit(int length);\\nstatic void insertion_sort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nstatic int median_of_three(const int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nstatic void partition_three_way(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int pivot,\\n                                int *equal_lo, int *equal_hi);\\nstatic void sift_down(int *toorder, int base, int root, int count);\\nstatic void heapsort_range(int *toorder, int lo, int hi);\\nstatic void _introsort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth_limit);\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\nstatic void _quicksort_parallel(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth_limit);\\n#endif\\n\\n/*\\n * A generic pRNG\\n */\\n#define MY_RAND_MAX 0x7FFFFFFF\\n\\n#define RANDNUM_W 521288629\\n#define RANDNUM_Z 362436069\\n\\nunsigned int randum_w = RANDNUM_W;\\nunsigned int randum_z = RANDNUM_Z;\\n\\nvoid srandnum(int seed)\\n{\\n    unsigned int w, z;\\n    w = (seed * 104623) & 0xffffffff;\\n    randum_w = (w) ? w : RANDNUM_W;\\n    z = (seed * 48947) & 0xffffffff;\\n    randum_z = (z) ? z : RANDNUM_Z;\\n}\\n\\ndouble randnum(void)\\n{\\n    unsigned int u;\\n    randum_z = 36969 * (randum_z & 65535) + (randum_z >> 16);\\n    randum_w = 18000 * (randum_w & 65535) + (randum_w >> 16);\\n    u = (randum_z << 16) + randum_w;\\n    return (abs(u));\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Main function\\n */\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\\n{\\n    int N = 0;\\n    int *our_list = NULL;\\n\\n    //The input provides the case size\\n    scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &N);\\n    if (N <= 0) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: please, provide the case size.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    //Generate the case\\n    our_list = generate_case(N);\\n    if (our_list == NULL) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: case instantiation failed.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    //Do the thing\\n    quicksort(our_list, N);\\n\\n    if (is_sorted(our_list, N) == 1) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error, for some reason list is still unsorted.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n#ifdef COMPUTE_MD5_PROBLEM\\n    //Compute MD5 Checksum for problem identification\\n    MD5_CTX c;\\n    unsigned char out[MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH];\\n    MD5_Init(&c);\\n    MD5_Update(&c, our_list, N * sizeof(int));\\n    MD5_Final(out, &c);\\n    for (int n = 0; n < MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH; n++) {\\n        printf(\\\"%02x\\\", out[n]);\\n    }\\n#endif\\n    printf(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n\\n    //Clean up\\n    free(our_list);\\n\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Public API\\n */\\nvoid quicksort(int *toorder, int N)\\n{\\n    if (N <= 1)\\n        return;\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n    if (N >= PARALLEL_SORT_LIMIT) {\\n        int depth_limit = sort_depth_limit(N);\\n#pragma omp parallel\\n        {\\n#pragma omp single\\n            {\\n                _quicksort_parallel(toorder, 0, N - 1, depth_limit);\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return;\\n    }\\n#endif\\n    _quicksort(toorder, 0, N - 1);\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Internal serial introsort. Recurse on the smaller partition and iterate\\n * over the larger one to limit stack use.\\n */\\nvoid _quicksort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    if (lo >= hi)\\n        return;\\n    _introsort(toorder, lo, hi, sort_depth_limit(hi - lo + 1));\\n}\\n\\nstatic int sort_depth_limit(int length)\\n{\\n    int depth = 0;\\n    while (length > 1) {\\n        length >>= 1;\\n        depth += 2;\\n    }\\n    return depth;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void insertion_sort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    for (int i = lo + 1; i <= hi; i++) {\\n        int value = toorder[i];\\n        int j = i;\\n        while (j > lo && toorder[j - 1] > value) {\\n            toorder[j] = toorder[j - 1];\\n            j--;\\n        }\\n        toorder[j] = value;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic int median_of_three(const int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;\\n    int a = toorder[lo];\\n    int b = toorder[mid];\\n    int c = toorder[hi];\\n\\n    if (a < b) {\\n        if (b < c)\\n            return b;\\n        return (a < c) ? c : a;\\n    }\\n    if (a < c)\\n        return a;\\n    return (b < c) ? c : b;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void partition_three_way(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int pivot,\\n                                int *equal_lo, int *equal_hi)\\n{\\n    int lt = lo;\\n    int i = lo;\\n    int gt = hi;\\n\\n    while (i <= gt) {\\n        if (toorder[i] < pivot) {\\n            swap(toorder, lt, i);\\n            lt++;\\n            i++;\\n        } else if (toorder[i] > pivot) {\\n            swap(toorder, i, gt);\\n            gt--;\\n        } else {\\n            i++;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    *equal_lo = lt;\\n    *equal_hi = gt;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void sift_down(int *toorder, int base, int root, int count)\\n{\\n    while (root < count / 2) {\\n        int child = root * 2 + 1;\\n        if (child + 1 < count &&\\n            toorder[base + child] < toorder[base + child + 1])\\n            child++;\\n        if (toorder[base + root] >= toorder[base + child])\\n            return;\\n        swap(toorder, base + root, base + child);\\n        root = child;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic void heapsort_range(int *toorder, int lo, int hi)\\n{\\n    int count = hi - lo + 1;\\n    for (int start = count / 2; start > 0; start--)\\n        sift_down(toorder, lo, start - 1, count);\\n    for (int end = count; end > 1; end--) {\\n        swap(toorder, lo, lo + end - 1);\\n        sift_down(toorder, lo, 0, end - 1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic void _introsort(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth_limit)\\n{\\n    while (lo < hi) {\\n        int length = hi - lo + 1;\\n        if (length <= INSERTION_SORT_CUTOFF) {\\n            insertion_sort(toorder, lo, hi);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n        if (depth_limit <= 0) {\\n            heapsort_range(toorder, lo, hi);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        depth_limit--;\\n        int equal_lo, equal_hi;\\n        int pivot = median_of_three(toorder, lo, hi);\\n        partition_three_way(toorder, lo, hi, pivot, &equal_lo, &equal_hi);\\n        int left_size = equal_lo - lo;\\n        int right_size = hi - equal_hi;\\n\\n        if (left_size < right_size) {\\n            if (left_size > 1)\\n                _introsort(toorder, lo, equal_lo - 1, depth_limit);\\n            lo = equal_hi + 1;\\n        } else {\\n            if (right_size > 1)\\n                _introsort(toorder, equal_hi + 1, hi, depth_limit);\\n            hi = equal_lo - 1;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n/*\\n * Task only large disjoint partitions; small ranges and exhausted paths use\\n * the serial introsort fallback.\\n */\\nstatic void _quicksort_parallel(int *toorder, int lo, int hi, int depth_limit)\\n{\\n    while (lo < hi) {\\n        int length = hi - lo + 1;\\n        if (length <= TASK_SORT_LIMIT || depth_limit <= 0) {\\n            _introsort(toorder, lo, hi, depth_limit);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        int equal_lo, equal_hi;\\n        int pivot = median_of_three(toorder, lo, hi);\\n        partition_three_way(toorder, lo, hi, pivot, &equal_lo, &equal_hi);\\n        int left_size = equal_lo - lo;\\n        int right_size = hi - equal_hi;\\n        int next_depth = depth_limit - 1;\\n\\n        if (left_size < TASK_SORT_LIMIT && right_size < TASK_SORT_LIMIT) {\\n            _introsort(toorder, lo, equal_lo - 1, next_depth);\\n            _introsort(toorder, equal_hi + 1, hi, next_depth);\\n            return;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (left_size >= right_size) {\\n            int task_lo = lo;\\n            int task_hi = equal_lo - 1;\\n            if (task_lo <= task_hi) {\\n#pragma omp task default(none) firstprivate(toorder, task_lo, task_hi, next_depth)\\n                {\\n                    _quicksort_parallel(toorder, task_lo, task_hi, next_depth);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            lo = equal_hi + 1;\\n        } else {\\n            int task_lo = equal_hi + 1;\\n            int task_hi = hi;\\n            if (task_lo <= task_hi) {\\n#pragma omp task default(none) firstprivate(toorder, task_lo, task_hi, next_depth)\\n                {\\n                    _quicksort_parallel(toorder, task_lo, task_hi, next_depth);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            hi = equal_lo - 1;\\n        }\\n        depth_limit = next_depth;\\n    }\\n}\\n#endif\\n\\n/*\\n * Swap two values.\\n */\\nvoid swap(int *toorder, int i, int j)\\n{\\n    int temp = toorder[i];\\n    toorder[i] = toorder[j];\\n    toorder[j] = temp;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Check if elements are in non-decreasing order\\n */\\nint is_sorted(int *toorder, int N)\\n{\\n    int has_inversion = 0;\\n    for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {\\n        has_inversion |= (toorder[i] < toorder[i - 1]);\\n    }\\n    return has_inversion;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Generate a case\\n */\\nint *generate_case(int N)\\n{\\n    int i;\\n    int *ret = NULL;\\n\\n    // Make case generation reproducible\\n    srandnum(0);\\n\\n    // Allocate memory\\n    ret = (int *) malloc(N * sizeof(int));\\n    if (ret == NULL) {\\n        printf(\\\"Error: some malloc won't work.\\\\n\\\");\\n        return NULL;\\n    }\\n    // Get pseudo-random positive integer values\\n    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) {\\n        ret[i] = drand(0, INT_MAX);\\n    }\\n    return ret;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * A pseudo-random number between two positive integer values\\n */\\ndouble drand(int xmin, int xmax)\\n{\\n    return xmin + (xmax - xmin) * randnum() / MY_RAND_MAX;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/quicksort.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Combining three-way median-of-three partitioning, bounded-depth heapsort fallback, small-range insertion sort, and coarse OpenMP tasks should make sorting robust and faster than the original Lomuto quicksort on large arrays while preserving the generated data and checksum.\",\"notes\":\"Integrates the measured three-way/task quicksort approach with introspective fallback and the adjacent-inversion reduction. Generator and PRNG code remain unchanged. No commands or local measurements were run; the controller should check correctness and end-to-end timing.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[\"213dc4953f734eab\",\"31711b2db43f40cd\",\"e78f66bf5b4e47c4\"],\"transformations\":[\"Replace sort-time shared-PRNG Lomuto partitioning with median-of-three three-way partitioning; preserve the case generator and its PRNG sequence.\",\"Use insertion sort for ranges up to 24 elements, recurse on the smaller side while iterating over the larger, and fall back to heapsort at an introspective depth limit.\",\"When OpenMP is enabled, start the team at 262144 elements, create tasks only for partitions of at least 32768 elements, and sort smaller ranges serially with a bounded-depth fallback.\",\"Use an OR reduction over adjacent-element inversion comparisons in is_sorted, preserving its any-inversion result.\"]}"}}
